Basically in order to ascend a tourist you're going to want to either
play carefully and use your advantages early on, or plan on getting
lucky. I've ascended tourists both ways.

I would say the best early priorities for a tourist are:

A) clearing out any shops on the low levels
B) carefully doing mines to build up a collection of daggers

B is necessary most of the time to successfully ascend a tourist.
Sometimes, rarely, you can get away with not getting a nice collection
of daggers, but this goes back to luck vs using resources. Daggers are
the best highly probable resource early on. 

I recommend sacrificing for frostbrand unless you're very rich on
wishes early on, in which case grayswandir is of course very wonderful
indeed (but if you're that rich in wishes you won't need anyone's
advice)

Frostbrand can be a little disappointing in that you will destroy
every potion that the monsters don't drink first, but I like it
anyhow. 

As far as wishing goes I recommend getting an SDSM for your first
wish. Your PYEC will provide one layer of MR, which is sufficient
until you wake the wizard; before which time you should find yourself
wearing a comr. 

In midgame I like this:

Frostbrand/Grayswandir
Silver Saber
SDSM
COMR
Gauntlets of Power
T-shirt
Boots of Speed

However later on, any time really between waking the wizard and
entering the first elemental plane, I like to switch to magicbane as
my primary weapon and wear a robe instead. 

I like this because quite simply I'm willing to give up damage output
for the ability to cast spells reasonably well for emergency type
situations. It's really a minor point because by this time you have a
pile of wands and virtually infinite charges (hooray pyec) you really
don't -need- to cast spells, but I personally like having the option.

On the other hand if you genocide everything people like to genocide
then you don't need to even consider this, because honestly I mostly
like having spells available to deal with the things I would nromally
genocide. 

Good luck with the tourist.

